course: dictionary
lesson: 6581
title: Ninety and the nineties
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Ninety is the number 90. It is nine tens, like nine piles of ten sweets. You can write it as 90 in figures or as the word ninety.
explain: «The nineties» is a noun for the numbers or ages from 90 to 99. If someone is in their nineties, they are between 90 and 99 years old. The word can also name the years of a century that end in 90 to 99.
explain: A ninety-degree angle is a right angle, a square corner like the corner of a book. In stories, «going ninety miles an hour» means going very fast. Always check the words around a number to see what it counts or measures.
fact: Ninety means 90, which is nine tens.
fact: «Devyanosto» is the Bulgarian word for ninety. It is an odd one, not built as «nine» plus «-ty», so it has to be learnt.
fact: «The nineties» means the numbers or ages from 90 to 99.
fact: A ninety-degree angle is a right angle, a square corner.
fact: In the Lost Sheep, a shepherd leaves ninety-nine sheep to look for one lost sheep.
exercise: «Some of Borneo's trees are over ninety metres tall.» How tall are some of the trees? | *Over ninety metres | Under nine metres | Over nine metres | Over nine hundred metres
exercise: What is a ninety-degree angle? | A straight line, like a ruler | A round circle | *A right angle, a square corner | A very sharp point
exercise: In the Lost Sheep, a shepherd leaves ninety-nine sheep to find one. How many sheep does he leave? | Nine hundred | *Ninety-nine | Ninety | One
test: Grandma says she is in her nineties. What does that mean? | She is 9 years old | *She is between 90 and 99 years old | She is 900 years old
test: In the story, «going ninety miles an hour» means what? | Going very slowly | *Going very fast | Standing still for ninety minutes
exam: Which word means 90? | Nineteen | Ninety-nine | *Ninety | Nine
